# Environment variables for REDI Sites.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development (`cp .env.example .env`) and
# never commit `.env` — it's already excluded in .gitignore.
#
# In production (Vercel), set these in the project dashboard under
# Settings -> Environment Variables. They are NOT read from a committed
# `.env` file in production; there isn't one.
#
# Every variable below is optional. With none set, the site builds and runs
# entirely from the local seed content in src/content/seed/ — this is the
# current default state of every environment, including production today.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORDPRESS_API_URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Headless WordPress origin (server-side, secret — never exposed to the
# browser). When set, every function in src/services/wordpress/*.ts attempts
# a real REST request to this origin before falling back to seed JSON; when
# unset (or the request fails), the seed fallback is used silently.
#
# Full API contract (expected endpoints, response shapes, required plugins/
# CPTs) is documented in docs/WORDPRESS_INTEGRATION.md and in the JSDoc atop
# each file in src/services/wordpress/.
#
# Example:
#   WORDPRESS_API_URL=https://cms.redisites.com
WORDPRESS_API_URL=
